#: ../../openmvcam/tutorial/image/transforms/perspective-correction.rst:2
msgid "Perspective correction"
msgstr "Perspektivkorrigering"

#: ../../openmvcam/tutorial/image/transforms/perspective-correction.rst:6
msgid ""
"The arbitrary 3-by-3 ``transform`` matrix is **only supported on the OpenMV "
"Cam N6** -- the keyword is silently ignored on every other board. "
"Applications that need to run anywhere else must use the canned "
":meth:`~image.Image.rotation_corr` method (with its ``corners=`` form) or "
"pre-compute the corrected image off-board."
msgstr ""
"Den godtyckliga 3-gånger-3-matrisen ``transform`` **stöds endast på OpenMV "
"Cam N6** -- nyckelordet ignoreras tyst på alla andra kort. Applikationer som"
" behöver kunna köras någon annanstans måste använda den färdiga metoden "
":meth:`~image.Image.rotation_corr` (med dess ``corners=``\\ -form) eller "
"förberäkna den korrigerade bilden utanför kortet."

#: ../../openmvcam/tutorial/image/transforms/perspective-correction.rst:15
msgid ""
"The canned :meth:`~image.Image.rotation_corr` method packages a particular "
"family of perspective warps behind a small set of parameters, and runs on "
"every supported board. Some applications need a warp that does not fit that "
"form: an arbitrary projective remap from one quadrilateral to another, a "
"calibrated correction for a known mounting that has already been worked out "
"off-line, a warp matrix handed over ready-made by some upstream algorithm. "
"For those, :meth:`~image.Image.draw_image` -- along with "
":meth:`~image.Image.copy`, :meth:`~image.Image.crop`, and "
":meth:`~image.Image.scale` -- accepts a ``transform`` keyword that takes a "
"hand-built 3-by-3 matrix describing the warp directly."
msgstr ""
"Den färdiga metoden :meth:`~image.Image.rotation_corr` paketerar en viss "
"familj av perspektivförvrängningar bakom en liten uppsättning parametrar och"
" körs på varje stött kort. Vissa applikationer behöver en förvrängning som "
"inte passar den formen: en godtycklig projektiv omavbildning från en "
"fyrhörning till en annan, en kalibrerad korrigering för ett känt fäste som "
"redan har räknats ut offline, eller en förvrängningsmatris som lämnats över "
"färdig av någon tidigare algoritm. För dessa accepterar "
":meth:`~image.Image.draw_image` -- tillsammans med "
":meth:`~image.Image.copy`\\ , :meth:`~image.Image.crop` och "
":meth:`~image.Image.scale` -- ett nyckelord ``transform`` som tar en "
"handbyggd 3-gånger-3-matris som direkt beskriver förvrängningen."

#: ../../openmvcam/tutorial/image/transforms/perspective-correction.rst:34
msgid "Affine and projective transformations"
msgstr "Affina och projektiva transformationer"

#: ../../openmvcam/tutorial/image/transforms/perspective-correction.rst:36
msgid ""
"Geometric warps are expressed in *homogeneous coordinates*: the pixel "
"position ``(x, y)`` with a ``1`` appended, multiplied by a 3-by-3 matrix."
msgstr ""
"Geometriska förvrängningar uttrycks i *homogena koordinater*\\ : "
"pixelpositionen ``(x, y)`` med en ``1`` tillagd, multiplicerad med en "
"3-gånger-3-matris."

#: ../../openmvcam/tutorial/image/transforms/perspective-correction.rst:41
msgid ""
"The *affine* form is the place to start. Its bottom row is fixed at "
":math:`(0, 0, 1)`:"
msgstr ""
"Den *affina* formen är platsen att börja på. Dess nedersta rad är fixerad "
"till :math:`(0, 0, 1)`\\ :"

#: ../../openmvcam/tutorial/image/transforms/perspective-correction.rst:44
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"\\begin{bmatrix} x' \\\\ y' \\\\ 1 \\end{bmatrix}\n"
"= \\begin{bmatrix} a & b & c \\\\ d & e & f \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 \\end{bmatrix}\n"
"  \\begin{bmatrix} x \\\\ y \\\\ 1 \\end{bmatrix}"
msgstr ""
"\\begin{bmatrix} x' \\\\ y' \\\\ 1 \\end{bmatrix}\n"
"= \\begin{bmatrix} a & b & c \\\\ d & e & f \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 \\end{bmatrix}\n"
"  \\begin{bmatrix} x \\\\ y \\\\ 1 \\end{bmatrix}"

#: ../../openmvcam/tutorial/image/transforms/perspective-correction.rst:50
msgid ""
"Written out, each output coordinate is a linear combination of the input "
"coordinates plus a constant:"
msgstr ""
"Utskrivet är varje utdatakoordinat en linjär kombination av "
"indatakoordinaterna plus en konstant:"

#: ../../openmvcam/tutorial/image/transforms/perspective-correction.rst:54
msgid ""
"x' = a x + b y + c, \\qquad\n"
"y' = d x + e y + f"
msgstr ""
"x' = a x + b y + c, \\qquad\n"
"y' = d x + e y + f"

#: ../../openmvcam/tutorial/image/transforms/perspective-correction.rst:59
msgid ""
"which covers scaling, rotation, shearing, and translation in any combination"
" -- and under all of them, parallel lines stay parallel."
msgstr ""
"vilket täcker skalning, rotation, skjuvning och translation i valfri "
"kombination -- och under alla dessa förblir parallella linjer parallella."

#: ../../openmvcam/tutorial/image/transforms/perspective-correction.rst:63
msgid "The *projective* (perspective) form frees the bottom row:"
msgstr "Den *projektiva* (perspektiv-) formen frigör den nedersta raden:"

#: ../../openmvcam/tutorial/image/transforms/perspective-correction.rst:66
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"\\begin{bmatrix} x'' \\\\ y'' \\\\ w' \\end{bmatrix}\n"
"= \\begin{bmatrix} a & b & c \\\\ d & e & f \\\\ g & h & 1 \\end{bmatrix}\n"
"  \\begin{bmatrix} x \\\\ y \\\\ 1 \\end{bmatrix},\n"
"\\qquad\n"
"(x', y') = \\left( \\frac{x''}{w'}, \\; \\frac{y''}{w'} \\right)"
msgstr ""
"\\begin{bmatrix} x'' \\\\ y'' \\\\ w' \\end{bmatrix}\n"
"= \\begin{bmatrix} a & b & c \\\\ d & e & f \\\\ g & h & 1 \\end{bmatrix}\n"
"  \\begin{bmatrix} x \\\\ y \\\\ 1 \\end{bmatrix},\n"
"\\qquad\n"
"(x', y') = \\left( \\frac{x''}{w'}, \\; \\frac{y''}{w'} \\right)"

#: ../../openmvcam/tutorial/image/transforms/perspective-correction.rst:74
msgid "Written out:"
msgstr "Utskrivet:"

#: ../../openmvcam/tutorial/image/transforms/perspective-correction.rst:76
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"x' = \\frac{a x + b y + c}{g x + h y + 1}, \\qquad\n"
"y' = \\frac{d x + e y + f}{g x + h y + 1}"
msgstr ""
"x' = \\frac{a x + b y + c}{g x + h y + 1}, \\qquad\n"
"y' = \\frac{d x + e y + f}{g x + h y + 1}"

#: ../../openmvcam/tutorial/image/transforms/perspective-correction.rst:81
msgid ""
"The division by :math:`w' = g x + h y + 1` is what makes the transformation "
"projective rather than merely affine. When :math:`g` and :math:`h` are both "
"zero, :math:`w'` stays at one and the division does nothing -- the affine "
"form again. When either is non-zero, :math:`w'` varies with the input "
"position and pixels at different positions get foreshortened by different "
"amounts, which no longer keeps parallel lines parallel -- it is exactly the "
"keystone effect of looking at a flat plane from an oblique angle. A "
"projective transformation is the most general geometric warp that takes "
"straight lines to straight lines; scaling, flipping, transposing, rotating, "
"and the four-corner rotation correction are all special cases of one."
msgstr ""
"Divisionen med :math:`w' = g x + h y + 1` är det som gör transformationen "
"projektiv snarare än bara affin. När :math:`g` och :math:`h` båda är noll "
"förblir :math:`w'` lika med ett och divisionen gör ingenting -- den affina "
"formen igen. När någondera är skild från noll varierar :math:`w'` med "
"indatapositionen och pixlar på olika positioner blir förkortade med olika "
"mycket, vilket inte längre håller parallella linjer parallella -- det är "
"precis den stupande effekten (keystone) av att titta på ett plant plan från "
"en sned vinkel. En projektiv transformation är den mest allmänna geometriska"
" förvrängning som tar raka linjer till raka linjer; skalning, spegling, "
"transponering, rotation och fyrhörnsrotationskorrigeringen är alla "
"specialfall av en sådan."

#: ../../openmvcam/tutorial/image/transforms/perspective-correction.rst:99
msgid ""
"The named transformations drop out of the affine form directly. The identity"
" transformation is the identity matrix, and:"
msgstr ""
"De namngivna transformationerna faller ut direkt ur den affina formen. "
"Identitetstransformationen är identitetsmatrisen, och:"

#: ../../openmvcam/tutorial/image/transforms/perspective-correction.rst:103
msgid ""
"\\underbrace{\\begin{bmatrix}\n"
"1 & 0 & t_x \\\\ 0 & 1 & t_y \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\n"
"\\end{bmatrix}}_{\\text{translate by } (t_x, \\; t_y)}\n"
"\\qquad\n"
"\\underbrace{\\begin{bmatrix}\n"
"s_x & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & s_y & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\n"
"\\end{bmatrix}}_{\\text{scale by } (s_x, \\; s_y)}\n"
"\\qquad\n"
"\\underbrace{\\begin{bmatrix}\n"
"\\cos\\theta & -\\sin\\theta & 0 \\\\\n"
"\\sin\\theta & \\cos\\theta & 0 \\\\\n"
"0 & 0 & 1\n"
"\\end{bmatrix}}_{\\text{rotate by } \\theta}"
msgstr ""
"\\underbrace{\\begin{bmatrix}\n"
"1 & 0 & t_x \\\\ 0 & 1 & t_y \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\n"
"\\end{bmatrix}}_{\\text{translate by } (t_x, \\; t_y)}\n"
"\\qquad\n"
"\\underbrace{\\begin{bmatrix}\n"
"s_x & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & s_y & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\n"
"\\end{bmatrix}}_{\\text{scale by } (s_x, \\; s_y)}\n"
"\\qquad\n"
"\\underbrace{\\begin{bmatrix}\n"
"\\cos\\theta & -\\sin\\theta & 0 \\\\\n"
"\\sin\\theta & \\cos\\theta & 0 \\\\\n"
"0 & 0 & 1\n"
"\\end{bmatrix}}_{\\text{rotate by } \\theta}"

#: ../../openmvcam/tutorial/image/transforms/perspective-correction.rst:119
msgid ""
"For most hand-built transforms an application starts with one of these as a "
"base and multiplies in further matrices for each additional operation, "
"ending with a single 3-by-3 matrix that describes the composite warp. "
"Matrices apply right to left: :math:`M = T R S` runs the scale first, then "
"the rotation, then the translation. The composite everyone needs eventually "
"is rotation about the image centre -- a bare rotation matrix spins the image"
" about the pixel origin at the top-left corner, so the centred version moves"
" the centre :math:`(c_x, c_y)` to the origin, rotates, and moves it back:"
msgstr ""
"För de flesta handbyggda transformer börjar en applikation med en av dessa "
"som bas och multiplicerar in ytterligare matriser för varje extra operation,"
" och slutar med en enda 3-gånger-3-matris som beskriver den sammansatta "
"förvrängningen. Matriser tillämpas från höger till vänster: :math:`M = T R "
"S` kör skalningen först, sedan rotationen, sedan translationen. Den "
"sammansättning som alla behöver så småningom är rotation kring bildens "
"centrum -- en bar rotationsmatris snurrar bilden kring pixelursprunget i det"
" övre vänstra hörnet, så den centrerade versionen flyttar centrum "
":math:`(c_x, c_y)` till ursprunget, roterar och flyttar tillbaka det:"

#: ../../openmvcam/tutorial/image/transforms/perspective-correction.rst:135
msgid ""
"M =\n"
"\\underbrace{\\begin{bmatrix}\n"
"1 & 0 & c_x \\\\ 0 & 1 & c_y \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\n"
"\\end{bmatrix}}_{\\text{move centre back}}\n"
"\\underbrace{\\begin{bmatrix}\n"
"\\cos\\theta & -\\sin\\theta & 0 \\\\\n"
"\\sin\\theta & \\cos\\theta & 0 \\\\\n"
"0 & 0 & 1\n"
"\\end{bmatrix}}_{\\text{rotate}}\n"
"\\underbrace{\\begin{bmatrix}\n"
"1 & 0 & -c_x \\\\ 0 & 1 & -c_y \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\n"
"\\end{bmatrix}}_{\\text{move centre to origin}}"
msgstr ""
"M =\n"
"\\underbrace{\\begin{bmatrix}\n"
"1 & 0 & c_x \\\\ 0 & 1 & c_y \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\n"
"\\end{bmatrix}}_{\\text{move centre back}}\n"
"\\underbrace{\\begin{bmatrix}\n"
"\\cos\\theta & -\\sin\\theta & 0 \\\\\n"
"\\sin\\theta & \\cos\\theta & 0 \\\\\n"
"0 & 0 & 1\n"
"\\end{bmatrix}}_{\\text{rotate}}\n"
"\\underbrace{\\begin{bmatrix}\n"
"1 & 0 & -c_x \\\\ 0 & 1 & -c_y \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\n"
"\\end{bmatrix}}_{\\text{move centre to origin}}"

#: ../../openmvcam/tutorial/image/transforms/perspective-correction.rst:151
msgid "The transform keyword"
msgstr "Nyckelordet transform"

#: ../../openmvcam/tutorial/image/transforms/perspective-correction.rst:153
msgid ""
"The matrix goes in through a ``transform`` keyword, supplied as a 3-by-3 "
":class:`ulab.numpy.ndarray <numpy.ndarray>`. The method to reach for is "
":meth:`~image.Image.draw_image`, which warps the source through the matrix "
"as it draws it onto a destination -- the result lands in a buffer the "
"application controls, and the warp composes with everything else on the "
"call: the scaling, the alpha blending, the masking."
msgstr ""
"Matrisen skickas in via ett nyckelord ``transform``\\ , angivet som en "
"3-gånger-3 :class:`ulab.numpy.ndarray <numpy.ndarray>`\\ . Metoden att ta "
"till är :meth:`~image.Image.draw_image`\\ , som förvränger källan genom "
"matrisen medan den ritar den på en destination -- resultatet hamnar i en "
"buffert som applikationen kontrollerar, och förvrängningen komponeras med "
"allt annat i anropet: skalningen, alfablandningen, maskeringen."

#: ../../openmvcam/tutorial/image/transforms/perspective-correction.rst:174
msgid ""
"The example warps ``img`` onto ``canvas`` scaled by 1.2 in each direction "
"and shifted left and up by 20 and 15 pixels respectively -- an affine warp "
"built directly from the matrix entries described above. The same keyword on "
":meth:`~image.Image.copy`, :meth:`~image.Image.crop`, and "
":meth:`~image.Image.scale` applies the warp to the image itself."
msgstr ""
"Exemplet förvränger ``img`` på ``canvas`` skalad med 1,2 i varje riktning "
"och förskjuten åt vänster och uppåt med 20 respektive 15 pixlar -- en affin "
"förvrängning byggd direkt från matriselementen som beskrivs ovan. Samma "
"nyckelord på :meth:`~image.Image.copy`\\ , :meth:`~image.Image.crop` och "
":meth:`~image.Image.scale` tillämpar förvrängningen på själva bilden."
